{
  "summary": "This experiment tested an RNA-only model using scgpt encoder in a multiprofile setup with avgpool aggregation, comparing against the scvi_n200 baseline (config_005). Validation accuracy (0.530) and F1 (0.515) are lower than the scvi_n200 baseline (0.650), suggesting scgpt may not improve performance in this configuration. Uncertainty remains about whether other factors, such as encoder-specific characteristics or hyperparameters, contributed to the difference, and how this compares to alternative encoders or aggregation strategies."
}

